 ### Compressive Rendering (Global Solver)
-A variant of global optimization specifically for reconstructing images from sparse pixel data [S2, unofficial]. It uses a gradient solver that operates on the entire image, as opposed to block-based approaches [S2, unofficial]. It is chosen when global consistency is more important than computational speed per iteration [S2, unofficial]. See [Neural Volume Rendering Training (MSE)](3429-neural-volume-rendering-training-mse.md).
